## 5. Exhaustive Unicode scalar sweep (`0x0000..0x10FFFF`, tables unchanged)

Verified `utf8_is_space`, `utf8_is_punct` (count and FNV-1a 64-bit hash over all matching code points), `utf8_encode` -> `utf8_iterate` round-trip, and `utf8_case_fold` (count and FNV-1a 64-bit hash over all changed code points and folded UTF-8 bytes) across all 1,114,112 code points (1,112,064 valid Unicode scalars) against the real `commonmark/src/buffer/cm_buffer.npk` and an independent Python oracle reading `commonmark/spec/case_fold.inc` (Unicode 16, 1,559 non-ASCII + 26 ASCII = 1,585 folds) and Unicode 15.0.0 P/S (matching cmark 0.31.2's `src/utf8.c`: 8,580 non-ASCII + 32 ASCII = 8,612 code points, excluding `U+2FFC..U+2FFF` and `U+31EF`):

